    <description>SE Phase 2: auto-tags Opportunity.Sales_Engineer__c from SE_Assignment__mdt when the tag is blank. Precedence: By Account (Account.Unique_Name__c CONTAINS an active By_Account Match_Key__c; if Unique_Name__c is blank, falls back to Account.Name CONTAINS the Match_Key__c) &gt; By AE (ONLY when Operation_Country__c = &apos;Indonesia&apos;: a Get Records lookup resolves $Record.OwnerId to its User, and that User&apos;s Username matches an active By_AE Match_Key__c — NOT the username of whoever is saving the record, so admin-driven Owner reassignment still tags correctly. If the Owner is an Indonesian AE but Operation Country is NOT Indonesia, By_AE is skipped and the opp falls through to By Country) &gt; By Country (Operation_Country__c matches an active By_Country Match_Key__c). Resolves SE_Username__c to an active User at runtime. REASSIGNMENT: on an already-tagged, OPEN (IsClosed=false) Opportunity UPDATE, the SE is cleared and the full precedence chain re-runs whenever Operation_Country__c changes OR OwnerId changes ($Record.Id not null guards against misreading insert-time $Record__Prior=null as a change). Once Closed Won/Lost the SE tag freezes. Account-side changes (Account_Tier__c / Unique_Name__c) are NOT visible to this Opportunity-triggered flow directly — see the companion Account_AfterSave_SEReassignTrigger flow, which blanks Sales_Engineer__c on open child Opportunities when those Account fields change, letting this flow&apos;s own blank-SE branch re-derive the tag. Edge case: if no rule matches after a reassignment, the SE is left blank.</description>
    <label>Opportunity - Before Save - Assign SE</label>
